--- answer ---
Found the bug in the `Resize` function at line 161. The loop uses `i <= diff` instead of `i < diff`, causing an off-by-one error. When `diff` is 0 (capacity >= current entries), it still loops once and evicts an entry.
Fixed. The bug was in `simplelru/lru.go:161` — the `Resize` function used `i <= diff` instead of `i < diff`, causing an off-by-one error that evicted one entry even when the new capacity was >= current entries (making `diff = 0`). Changed to `<` so zero entries are evicted when capacity is sufficient. All tests pass.